    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now the question mark hides inside operations:\n\n(? − 2763) ÷ 86 × 13 = 208\n\nPeel from the outside, reversing BODMAS.\n\nThe last outside step was × 13, so undo it:\n\n(? − 2763) ÷ 86 = 208 ÷ 13 = 16",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Next layer, ÷ 86. Undo it:\n\n? − 2763 = 16 × 86 = 1376\n\nLast layer, − 2763. Undo it:\n\n? = 1376 + 2763 = 4139\n\nEach peel uses the opposite operation, outside-in.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
